(7238817, 1120201, 60173, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Cuttooth:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Garry:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice shot, Mark. How close a representation is the green water to what it was in reality? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Garry (and everyone) for the comments.  The water is actually that murky green color.  I''m thinking probably due to the algae content in it. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It''s also overcast. Had the blue skies been out, there may have been more blue. Maybe... :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Cuttooth: Originally posted by Garry: Nice shot, Mark. How close a representation is the green water to what it was in reality?   Thanks Garry (and everyone) for the comments.  The water is actually that murky green color.  I''m thinking probably due to the algae content in it.   It''s also overcast. Had the blue skies been out, there may have been more blue. Maybe... :)', '2014-07-08 17:28:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7238819, 1120201, 96574, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aliqui:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Cuttooth:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Garry:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice shot, Mark. How close a representation is the green water to what it was in reality? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Garry (and everyone) for the comments.  The water is actually that murky green color.  I''m thinking probably due to the algae content in it. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It''s also overcast. Had the blue skies been out, there may have been more blue. Maybe... :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yep, true.  It was quite cloudy that morning.</td>', 'Originally posted by aliqui: Originally posted by Cuttooth: Originally posted by Garry: Nice shot, Mark. How close a representation is the green water to what it was in reality?   Thanks Garry (and everyone) for the comments.  The water is actually that murky green color.  I''m thinking probably due to the algae content in it.   It''s also overcast. Had the blue skies been out, there may have been more blue. Maybe... :)   Yep, true.  It was quite cloudy that morning.', '2014-07-08 17:33:07.000000', NULL, 0),
